    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0510" n="414" xml:id="pg414"/>

                <head>No. 307.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Nelson</hi>,</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-04-13"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 13,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 237.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Attorney General has addressed a letter
                    to this Department under date of the 5th instant, covering a “report” of the
                    grand jury of the United States district court of Texas, relative to the
                    depredations perpetrated upon citizens of that State by persons coming from the
                    Mexican side of the Rio Grande. Copies of these papers are inclosed herewith.
                    You are requested to lay them before the minister for foreign affairs, to
                    remonstrate earnestly against the outrages therein alleged, and to demand
                    redress for them.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d307-a1.xml" xpointer="d307-a1"/>
